Microsoft Excel

Excel is important enough that I'd make it its own technical-skill category:

    Microsoft Excel
    Spreadsheet creation and maintenance
    Financial spreadsheets
    Data entry and manipulation
    Basic Excel formulas
    Sorting and filtering
    Formatting financial data
    Working with accounting data
    Spreadsheet reconciliation

Important: I would not put advanced Excel skills such as PivotTables, XLOOKUP, INDEX/MATCH, Power Query, VBA, etc. into the 75–100% group unless your research specifically found them at that frequency. Those are useful skills, but they're more appropriate as preferred/secondary skills.
Accounting / ERP Systems

At this frequency level, I'd list the category rather than claiming that one specific software is universal:

    Accounting software
